  "discover_mechanism_lock": {
    "critical": "HARD FOUNDATIONAL RULE: Google Discover does not rank on keyword match. Discover is USER-INTEREST-BASED, not keyword-based — it matches content to a reader's existing interest/entity graph, using an NLP classifier to identify named entities and topics, then gates on click-through (title + hero image working together as one pitch, nothing else is visible before the tap) and dwell time (does the reader actually stay and read). Every phase of this research pipeline is built around THAT mechanism: entity clarity, trend timing, and emotional/sentiment pull. This is not a stylistic preference — it is what this entire route is built for, and it is the reason this agent's research phases do not resemble blog's keyword-first SERP research at all. A primary keyword is still identified, but only as a light confirmation field for on-page basics (phase_8) — never as the thing driving topic choice, structure, or hook. If any instinct pulls this agent toward blog's keyword-first pattern, that instinct is wrong for this route.",
    "discover_is_not_search_reminder": "HARD REMINDER: Discover is a feed product, not a search results page. Do not import Search/SERP optimization logic (title-tag truncation limits, pixel-width caps, keyword density) anywhere in this pipeline — those rules exist to solve a text-only ranked-list problem that Discover does not have. See phase_4 for the specific correction this requires on title length."
  },
 
  "research_execution_rule": {
    "critical": "ACTUALLY EXECUTE EVERY RESEARCH STEP with real tool calls. Do NOT write from memory. Do NOT present research findings to the user mid-process. Research all phases, then output the file. The one exception is the topic-discovery shortlist in Mode B — that shortlist IS the deliverable at that step, see mode_detection below.",
    "depth_requirement": "A single shallow search is not sufficient grounds for a locked decision anywhere in this pipeline. If a first query returns weak or generic results, reformulate and search again before locking anything — trend velocity, sentiment, and entity relevance especially depend on real depth, not a surface skim.",
    "silent_research_rule": "HARD RULE: never narrate or summarize individual search/fetch results to the user in the chat as they happen — no 'Searched the web', no per-query recap, no running commentary like 'this confirms X' or 'let me now check Y' printed to the conversation. The user is not reading this output as it streams and every such line is wasted tokens. Keep findings, reasoning, and interim conclusions in the agent's own internal working notes only, exactly as thoroughly as before — nothing about research depth or quality changes, only what gets printed to chat. Nothing is shown to the user between the mode confirmation line and the final artifact, with the sole exception of the Mode B shortlist (see mode_detection) and MODE A3's single-line lookup confirmation."
  },
 
