      "mutual_exclusivity": "Never select both. If somehow both angles seem present, pick whichever is the stronger, more specific fit and skip the other.",
      "poll_research_requirement": "If Poll is selected: the question and both/all options must come from the actual research (phase_1's specific_frustration_or_desire and sentiment findings) — a real split the audience actually has, phrased in their terms, not an invented generic either/or.",
      "quiz_research_requirement": "If Quiz is selected: this is a genuine research output, not a templated fill-in. The quiz STYLE (diagnostic 'is this right for you' vs. recommendation 'which look are you') is determined by what phase_1 actually found — diagnostic fits when the research shows readers uncertain whether something suits them; recommendation fits when the research shows readers wanting to be sorted into one of several genuine, distinct options. The questions, answer options, and final results must all be built from real audience findings from phase_1 — actual variations in taste/situation/preference that showed up in research, not invented placeholder branches.",
