  "phase_7_linking": {
    "objective": "Compile the link list for this post. Internal links arrive pre-decided from upstream (Mode A2) or are omitted (Mode A/B one-off topics with no batch context). This agent's own live research in this phase covers EXTERNAL links only.",
    "total_cap": "2-3 internal + 2-3 external maximum. Hard ceiling, natural placement.",
    "internal_links": {
      "mode_a2_source": "If this topic arrived via Mode A2 (Bucket Explorer JSON), its internal_links object (links_to / linked_from, each with anchor_context) is consumed directly and verbatim. No live search, no re-derivation, no substitution — even if this agent's own reading of the topic suggests a different internal link would fit better, the given links are used as-is.",
      "mode_a_or_b_source": "If this topic arrived via Mode A (plain topic) or Mode B (trend scan pick) with no Bucket Explorer JSON, there are no pre-assigned internal links. Internal links are omitted from section_8 entirely in this case, UNLESS the user separately and explicitly supplies specific internal links to use for this one-off post. This agent does NOT perform its own live internal-link discovery under any mode — that capability has moved entirely to the Bucket Explorer prompt.",
      "anchor_text_rule": "Descriptive and authority-passing — the reader should understand exactly where they're going from the anchor alone. Where anchor_context arrived from the Bucket Explorer JSON, use it to inform natural anchor text placement; do not just paste the anchor_context verbatim as anchor text unless it already reads naturally as such."
